To find out how many miles Jeff walks in a week, we first calculate the distance for a single round trip (there and back). Since the office is 3 miles away, a round trip is \(3 \text{ miles} \times 2 = 6 \text{ miles}\).

Jeff works 5 times a week, so the total distance he walks in a week is \(6 \text{ miles/trip} \times 5 \text{ trips} = 30 \text{ miles}\).

\boxed{30}

Since Becky ate 10 slices and she ate 3 more slices than Jake did, Jake ate 10 - 3 = 7 slices. Silvia ate twice as many slices as Jake did, so Silvia ate 2 * 7 = 14 slices. 

The total number of slices eaten by all three is 10 (Becky) + 7 (Jake) + 14 (Silvia) = 31 slices.

\boxed{31}

John has 3 children, and he buys 2 pairs of shoes for each child. So the total number of pairs of shoes he buys is 3 * 2 = 6 pairs.

Each pair of shoes costs $60, so the total cost is 6 * $60 = $360.

\boxed{360}

Alexandra raises $430. Kim raises $320 more than Alexandra, so Kim raises $430 + 320 = 750$. Sarah raises $300. Maryam raises $400 more than Sarah, so Maryam raises $300 + 400 = 700$. 

The total amount of money they raised is $430 + 750 + 300 + 700 = 2180$ dollars.

\boxed{2180}

Tom gets 4 car washes a month, and there are 12 months in a year. So, the total number of car washes in a year is 4 * 12 = 48 car washes.

Each car wash costs $15, so the total amount Tom pays in a year is 48 * 15 = $720.

\boxed{720}

On Monday, Robert collects 20 shells. Since Kylie collects 5 more shells than Robert, Kylie collects 20 + 5 = 25 shells on Monday.

On Tuesday, Kylie collects 2 times more shells than she did on Monday. So, Kylie collects 2 * 25 = 50 shells on Tuesday.

\boxed{50}

Larry has 3 cats. Since he has 3 times as many dogs as cats, he has 3 * 3 = 9 dogs. He has 2 fewer rabbits than dogs, so he has 9 - 2 = 7 rabbits. The number of fish in his tank is three times the number of rabbits, which is 3 * 7 = 21 fish. Larry's collection of gerbils is 1/3 the number of fish, so he has 21 / 3 = 7 gerbils.

To find the total number of pets Larry has, we add up all the animals: 3 cats + 9 dogs + 7 rabbits + 21 fish + 7 gerbils = 47.

\boxed{47}

Since Suzy’s iPhone is 1 year old, Ben’s iPhone is 2 times older, which means Ben’s iPhone is 1 * 2 = 2 years old.

Brandon’s iPhone is four times as old as Ben’s iPhone, so Brandon’s iPhone is 4 * 2 = 8 years old.

