To find the total volume of the hole, we multiply the length, width, and depth: \(6 \, \text{ft} \times 4 \, \text{ft} \times 3 \, \text{ft} = 72 \, \text{cubic feet}\).

Given that it takes Bob 3 seconds to shovel a cubic foot of earth, the total time required to shovel 72 cubic feet is: \(72 \, \text{cubic feet} \times 3 \, \text{seconds/cubic foot} = 216 \, \text{seconds}\).

\boxed{216}

Since Samantha has 27 paintings and she has 12 fewer paintings than Shelley, Shelley has 27 + 12 = 39 paintings.

Shelley has 8 paintings more than Kim, so Kim has 39 - 8 = 31 paintings.

